From ce46dc5bbe1587a85d1cb7af2afa37e32b292fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:32:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): hub-admission-denied cards keep the
 worker queue across a gateway restart; self-check repins stranded
 worker-first cards

Incident (11-13, hermes-hub, t_01a1d2a8ea3dfbdb): kanban_create reported a denied card placed on the
pool but stored it worker-first with runs_on NULL. It sat ready 36 min while pool workers claimed 63
other cards, until a manual `hermes kanban move --pool`.

Cause: every gateway restart records the sync loop "stopped" (kanban_sync_runstate), and the new loop
cleared that only after its first completed round, which took ~20 min on the hub after a restart
(02:02:46 -> 02:23:05). In that window the tool's machine check (`not runstate.down()`) read the worker
queue as unreachable, so pool_route fell back to worker-first. Every denied card created 00:56-02:21
was worker-first, each just after a restart; those before and after queued.

- kanban_sync_runstate.started(): a loop that passed its start checks drops an earlier loop's
  graceful-stop record. Crash and start-refusal records still wait for a completed round.
- Dispatcher self-check (kanban_worker_first_selfcheck, from reevaluate): a ready worker-first card
  created here with runs_on NULL, no claim/lease, ready >= 5 min, on a gateway whose worker queue a
  live machine carries for the card's labels, gets the same Board repin `kanban move --pool` makes
  ([pool:worker, *coordination labels]); logged at WARNING and recorded on its moved event.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pool_deny_runs_on.py (create through the denied path during a
restarted loop's first round: runs_on set locally and on the fake Board; self-check repin and its
non-cases). Red on main: 3 of 8 fail.
